  <heading>CFLTHS (immediate)</heading>
  <desc>
    <brief>
      <para>Compare unsigned higher than or same as immediate and fault</para>
    </brief>
    <authored>
      <para>This instruction compares the unsigned value in a register with an
immediate, and generates a Conditional fault exception
if the register value is higher than or the same as the immediate.
If an exception is generated, the <syntax>&lt;reason&gt;</syntax> operand
  is copied to <xref linkend="ESR_ELx">ESR_ELx</xref>.</para>
      <para>This instruction does not affect the condition flags.</para>
    </authored>
  </desc>
